  <xs:simpleType name="msCapabilitiesT">
    <xs:annotation >
      <xs:documentation >
        MS hardware respectively CUPPS platform capabilities to do PCI-DSS
        compliant masking of PAN and other credit card data.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="FOID11">
        <xs:annotation >
          <xs:documentation >
            Implementing the IATA FOID Addendum 1.1 algorithm detailed in the 
            CUSS spec or a compliant algorithm in the hardware of the MS device.
            Thus all apps and platform are out-of-scope for PCI-DSS. Sample 
            implementation with international patents done by Objective Solutions 
            in Stockholm in their SCR 100 device.
          </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="NoMasking">
        <xs:annotation >
          <xs:documentation >
            No implementation in the MS hardware for masking, also no implementation
            for masking at the CUPPS platform level, which must then be PCI-DSS 
            compliant and requieres CUPPS applications using the MS device to also
            be PCI-DSS compliant.
          </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="PlatformOnly">
        <xs:annotation >
          <xs:documentation >
            No implementation in the MS hardware for masking, but masking is
            done at the CUPPS plattform level which must then be PCI-DSS compliant.
          </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="MaskOnOff">
        <xs:annotation >
          <xs:documentation >
            MS hardware allows for masking, but can also be configured by the 
            platform on a per CUPPS application basis to not mask the MS track 
            data, in which case the CUPPS plattform and the CUPPS application
            then must be PCI-DSS compliant. Switching the MS hardware is done
            during processing of the deviceLockRequest.
          </xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>


